action,x,y,origin,button,key,micros,note,platform
# P108 on Windows WinUIBackend: a held drag, then a throw, after the app's own FREE and BOUND.
# The card is 40x40 at frame x 21-61, y 130-170 DIPs (display at 125%), measured on the WinUI capture of 2026-10-19.
# HOLD comes FIRST, from where STEPS DONE leaves the card (offset 0): press its centre, drag 20, hold 0.3 s, release in
# place. Pass: a DRAG release 20 on with velocity 0 and HOLD, no coast. The card is then at offset 20, a known place.
# THROW from there: 5 per move with 16 ms sleeps, released in place. Pass: release velocity within 1 pt/s of the speed
# over the last 0.1 s of the points as received; coast on the closed form within 0.01 pt; end = release + v*0.4995.
# The macOS file throws first and holds where the throw stopped; that place varies with the throw, and the hold missed
# the card on both Windows backends (2026-10-19), hence this order. Mouseups go in place: with a position, the
# synthesiser's move and checks delayed the release past the 0.1 s the velocity is measured over.
# 2026-10-19 WinUI: pass -- HOLD released at 20.00 with velocity 0, no coast; THROW released at 70.40 at 51.1 pt/s (51.1 over the last 0.1 s), coast on the closed form to 95.91.
# P108(Windows):先「停住」再「拋擲」,讓兩次按下都落在已知位置的卡片上;通過條件見上方英文。
sleep,,,,,,11000000,FREE and BOUND run first,windows
